\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-180\li180\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Jesus, still lead on,\cf0 
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0 Till our rest be won,
\par And, although the way be cheerless,
\par We will follow, calm and fearless;
\par Guide us by Thy hand
\par To our fatherland.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-180\li180\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. If the way be drear,
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0 If the foe be near,
\par Let not faithless fears o'ertake us,
\par Let not faith and hope forsake us;
\par For, through many a foe,
\par To our home we go.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-135\li180\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  3. When we seek relief
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0\qj  From a long-felt grief,
\par  When oppressed by new temptations,
\par  Lord, increase and perfect patience;
\par  Show us that bright shore
\par  Where we weep no more.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-180\li180\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par   4.  Jesus, still lead on,
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0   Till our rest be won;
\par   Heavenly Leader, still direct us,
\par   Still support, console, protect us,
\par   Till we safely stand
\par \pard      In our fatherland.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

